SavanXP

Experimental system, usable for tests from the shell.

Current i386 path:
- GRUB2/Multiboot2 BIOS boot
- Framebuffer text console and PS/2 canonical TTY
- Syscalls, processes and the reference userland shell
- /disk as the main persistent volume

Useful commands:
- help: commands and examples
- sysinfo: system diagnostics
- df: total, used and free space on /disk
- cd /disk: enter the persistent volume
- pwd: show the current directory
- ls: list the current directory
- sync: flush filesystem metadata

Notes:
- /README lives in the initramfs
- /disk/README lives in persistent SxFS
- External programs in /disk/bin can be launched from the shell
